<Base title="Terms of Use" description="Terms of Use of Talha M Blog: the rules for reading, sharing and commenting on our content, our newsletter terms, and how copyright takedown requests work.">
  <section class="article-head"><h1>Terms of Use</h1></section>
  <div class="prose">
<p><em>Last updated: October 16, 2026 — 11:53 PM (Pakistan time)</em></p>
    <p>Welcome to Talha M Blog (talhablog.com). These Terms of Use explain the rules that apply when you read, share, comment on or otherwise use this website. By using this website, you accept these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the website.</p>

    <h2>What this website is</h2>
    <p>Talha M Blog is an independent news and information website that publishes news explanations, background articles and life stories in simple English. It is free to read, and it is operated by Talha Mehmood, an independent publisher based in Pakistan. You can learn more on our <a href="/about/">About page</a>. You do not need an account to read this website; comments and the email newsletter are optional features. How information is handled on this website is explained in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, and the limits of the information we publish are explained in our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.</p>

    <h2>Using our content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You may read our articles freely for personal use and learning.</li>
      <li>You may share links to our articles on social media, in messages, or on your own website.</li>
      <li>You may quote a short part of an article if you name Talha M Blog as the source and include a working link to the original article.</li>
      <li>You may not copy a full article, or a large part of one, and publish it elsewhere as your own work.</li>
      <li>You may not sell our articles, or include them in a paid product, without our written permission.</li>
      <li>The Talha M Blog name, logo and our illustrations belong to Talha M Blog unless a page says otherwise. News facts belong to no one; the words and pictures we create to explain them are ours.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Comments</h2>
    <p>Most stories have a comments section. To comment, you type a name, an email address and your comment; you may also add a website link. You do not create an account, and there is no password. Your chosen name and your comment appear publicly under the story; your email address is never shown publicly. Comments appear <b>immediately</b> when you post them — they are not held for approval first. By commenting, you agree to these rules:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Be respectful. Disagreement is welcome; abuse, hate speech and personal attacks are not.</li>
      <li>Do not post anything unlawful, threatening, defamatory or misleading, and do not present rumours about a person as if they were proven facts.</li>
      <li>Do not post spam, advertisements, or repeated copies of the same comment.</li>
      <li>Do not impersonate another person, and do not publish another person's private information, such as a phone number, home address or email address.</li>
      <li>Do not post text or images that belong to someone else unless you have their permission.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for your comment, for its content, and for the results of posting it.</li>
      <li>By commenting, you allow Talha M Blog to display your comment under your chosen name for as long as the story remains published.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We read comments after they appear. We may hide or delete any comment that breaks these rules, and we may block repeat offenders from commenting. We are not required to keep every comment published. The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what comment information is stored (including your IP address and browser type, kept for spam and security protection) and how you can ask for your own comment to be deleted. If you believe a comment about you is unfair or unlawful, email us through our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> and we will review it.</p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>Readers may subscribe to our free email newsletter through the sign-up box on story pages. You enter your email address and then confirm it by clicking the link in the confirmation email we send you (this double confirmation is called double opt-in). The newsletter is run for us by Kit, and it contains new stories and, rarely, an important website announcement.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Every newsletter email contains an unsubscribe link. You may leave the list at any time, free of charge, with one click.</li>
      <li>We never sell or rent subscriber email addresses. The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how newsletter addresses are handled.</li>
      <li>We may change or stop the newsletter. If we stop it, subscriber addresses will be removed from the newsletter list.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information, not professional advice</h2>
    <p>Everything published on Talha M Blog is for general information and education. Our articles summarise and explain news and public information; they are not legal, medical, financial or other professional advice, and they are not a substitute for advice from a qualified professional. For decisions about health, money, legal matters or safety, please consult a qualified professional or an official source. Our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> explains this in more detail.</p>

    <h2>Accuracy and changes to articles</h2>
    <p>We work hard to check facts and keep articles current. Even so, news can develop quickly, official figures can change, and early reports may be incomplete or later corrected. We cannot promise that every detail is complete and current at every moment. When we learn that an article needs a correction or an important update, we change it and show an "Updated" date on the article. The current version of an article replaces its earlier versions.</p>

    <h2>Fair and lawful use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not use this website for any unlawful purpose.</li>
      <li>Do not try to break, overload, scan or gain unauthorised access to this website, its server or any accounts connected with it.</li>
      <li>Do not copy our content automatically in bulk in a way that harms the website. Normal indexing of our public pages by search engines is welcome.</li>
      <li>Do not impersonate Talha M Blog, or use its name to mislead readers about a page, an account or a product.</li>
      <li>Do not use the comments, or any other feature of this website, to send spam or mass unsolicited messages.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Copyright and takedown requests</h2>
    <p>We write our articles in our own words and create our own illustrations. If you believe that text or an image on this website uses your material without permission, please email contact@talhablog.com with the subject "Copyright" and include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your full name, and the name of the owner of the material if that is a different person.</li>
      <li>The exact address (URL) of the page on talhablog.com where the material appears.</li>
      <li>A short description of your material and, if possible, a link to where it was first published.</li>
      <li>A statement that you own the material, or are authorised to act for its owner, and that its use on this website is not permitted.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to reply to complete requests within a few working days. If a request checks out, we will remove or correct the material as quickly as reasonably possible. If you sent a request by mistake, or you later give permission, email us again and we will restore the material where appropriate. The same process is described on our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Our articles link to other websites as sources and for further reading. Those websites have their own owners, terms and privacy policies, and they may change without our knowledge. A link from Talha M Blog is not an endorsement of everything on the linked website, and we are not responsible for the content, accuracy or policies of external websites.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>This website has applied to display advertising provided by Google AdSense and similar services, and advertisements will appear once the application is approved. Our application is currently under review, Auto ads is switched on, and no advertisements are shown yet. When advertising starts, advertisements will be selected automatically by Google's systems. The appearance of an advertisement does not mean that we recommend the advertised product, service or company, and any purchase or agreement you make with an advertiser is entirely between you and that advertiser. Consent messages about advertising cookies may be shown to visitors in the regions where they apply; our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains this in full.</p>

    <h2>Availability of the website</h2>
    <p>We try to keep this website available at all times, but we cannot guarantee uninterrupted access. The website may be unavailable for a time because of maintenance, technical problems or reasons outside our control. We may change, move or remove articles, categories or parts of the website at any time.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of responsibility</h2>
    <p>To the extent allowed by law, Talha M Blog and its operator are not responsible for loss or damage resulting from reliance on information published on this website, from the website being unavailable, or from the content of external websites. Readers use the information here at their own judgement. Nothing in these terms removes any responsibility that cannot legally be removed.</p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We may update these Terms of Use from time to time, for example when a feature of the website changes. When we do, the revised terms will be posted on this page with a new "Last updated" date, and they will apply from that date. By continuing to use the website after a change, you accept the updated terms.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Pakistan. If any single part of these terms is found unenforceable, the remaining parts continue to apply in full.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have any question about these Terms of Use, please email us at <a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com">contact@talhablog.com</a> or use our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>

